/-
  The tie (C14) on `f2-examples/e2-equation.kompile.kore`, the kompiled text of construct fixture e2-equation
  (`test/constructs/fixtures/e2-equation`), sentence by sentence, against the translation of the text as
  written (`trS ad := trAxiom k.symbolDecls k.aliasNames ad`), on the literals `kore` and `defn`, for
  every interpretation H. Nothing here reads `Parse.parse` or `emit`. Written by
  `test/constructs/tiegen.py e2-equation`; run from the package root: `lake env lean -j1 test/TieE2Equation.lean`.

  Layer 1.
  - `wf_defn`: `wf defn = true`.
  - The account: the class lists partition the 260 sentences of the user module E2-EQUATION, in
    `tieClasses`' order (`account`, `account_sizes`, `account_classes`); the no-direction class holds
    exactly the sentences that apply a symbol Γ lacks (`account_absent`, `absent_closed`).
  - `absent_proj_below`: the 13 no-direction sentences that are equations of a projection
    `project:X` are of sorts X that are K, KItem or below KItem in Γ (`GenEqs.projBelowB`).
  - `attrs_agree`: the attributes the translation does not read agree with `defn`.
  - `sig_origin_but_next`: each of the 209 items of `sigItems c` but one is a declaration's item
    of the text or a surplus one; the one is next's arity at the configuration sort, which Γ states
    and the text, having no `\rewrites` (`text_nextless`), does not. `decls_entailed`: Γ entails
    the item of each declaration without sort parameters of a symbol Γ has (by ranges of the lists).
  - The definition reads no confined sort (`readsConfined_c`), has no open generator (`noRaw`), owes
    no fact (`term_named`, `total_named`, `agree_named`, `match_named`) and no rule's or clause's
    condition (`owed_rules`, `owed_clauses`), so Γ with the step's closure has a model for every
    H (`consistent`).

  Layer 2, by class (indices are the text's axiom numbers, `AxiomDecl.index`).
  - Function equations (33) and priority equations (4), in the order `fnText` lists them
    (`fns_account`): each of Γ's items but 0, 2, 3, 4, 8 is the translation of one sentence
    (`shape`), so Γ entails it (`fns_entailed`). Items 0 (200), 2 (202), 3 (203), 8 (210) (sentence
    in parentheses) are the clause under the negation of the clauses of a smaller priority that are
    not `aside`, which the sentence entails (`prio<j>_w1`, W1) and is without that premise
    (`prio<j>_text`). Item 4 (204) and its sentence agree up to the order of the operands of their
    sorted disjunctions and the names of their variables (`ac<j>_same`, `TieAlpha.acEqB`), so they
    are satisfied by the same interpretations (`ac<j>_iff`) and Γ entails the sentence.
    `fns_from_text` (the converse), `fn_prios` (the priorities the sentences state are the
    clauses').
  - Constructor sentences (24): entailed by Γ (`cons_entailed`).
  - No junk (3 of a sort without generators, `nojunk_trivial_entailed`; 6 equal to
    one of Γ's constructor items, `nojunk_items`; 1 KItem's with its disjuncts in the text's
    order, `nojunk_kitem_entailed`).
  - Set idempotence (60): Γ with it has no model (`idem_refuted`).
  - Library sample, 157 (`I -Int 0 = I`): holds at values (`lib166`, `lib166_at_values`).
  - The converse over Γ's content: each premise is a consequence of the function sentences (200,
    202, 203, 210 through W1, 204 through `ac4_iff`), Γ's rule items, the five parts Γ defines by
    predicates, or definedness (`gamma_from`).
  - Function functional: at values in every model of `Γc`, from the sort predicates' results, not
    from `FnHyp` (`fnFun_at_values`, `fnFun_account`).
  - Hooked functional, collection law, library: at values (no theorem here); no direction:
    `absent_closed`.

  The sentences with no counterpart in f2-examples/ens.kompile.kore are `unmapped` (12);
  the sentences of a class with a theorem that no theorem here holds of are `uncovered` (0).
-/
import KcoreSpec

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option maxRecDepth 1000000

namespace KCore.TieE2Equation

open KCore ML Faithful KoreAML

kore_term kore from "f2-examples/e2-equation.kompile.kore"
definition_of defn from "f2-examples/e2-equation.kompile.kore"
user_axioms U from "f2-examples/e2-equation.kompile.kore" module "E2-EQUATION"

noncomputable abbrev c : Semantics := defn.sem
noncomputable abbrev cH (H : HookParams) : Semantics := c.withHooks H

/-- No parameter of the definition is an open generator. -/
theorem noRaw : ∀ k ∈ c.params, k.raw = false := by decide +kernel

/-- The definition reads no confined sort: its theory is Γ. -/
theorem readsConfined_c : c.readsConfined = false := by decide +kernel

/-- The axioms of the user module, in text order. -/
noncomputable def userAxioms : List AxiomDecl := kore.axiomDecls.filter (·.module == "E2-EQUATION")

theorem userAxioms_eq : userAxioms = U.all := by kernel_rfl
theorem userAxioms_length : U.all.length = 260 := by decide +kernel

/-- `tr s`: the item `Theory.ofDefinition kore` holds for the sentence. -/
noncomputable def trS (ad : AxiomDecl) : Item := trAxiom kore.symbolDecls kore.aliasNames ad

theorem trS_is_text : (Theory.ofDefinition kore).axioms = kore.axiomDecls.map trS := rfl

/-! ## Layer 1 -/

set_option maxHeartbeats 1000000 in
theorem coreOK : c.coreOK = true := by decide_cheap
theorem coreOKH (H : HookParams) : (cH H).coreOK = true := (Semantics.coreOK_withHooks c H).trans coreOK

